//! flags: -p ssa

// The loop over a node's children vectorized: the program and schedule of
// child-volumes-sorted.bonsai with `.vectorize(tris.Interior.children)`
// between the sort and the loopify, which makes the parent's test of its
// four children -- the mask bit and the sort key per child -- one test of
// all four at once, Embree's `intersectNode` of an AABBNode.
//
// What to read for. The children's boxes are stored by component, a vector
// of four `vec3f` that is one vector per component (`lo`, `hi`), and each
// lane of the gang tests one child: so a lane's box is the stored vectors
// themselves, reinterpreted as the gang's per-lane `vec3f`,
//
//     let _tN = reinterpret_cast<f32x3$v4>(lo) in
//
// and not a chain of selects over the four, which is what a computed index
// into a short vector becomes. The ray is uniform and broadcast
// (`f32x4(rdir.x)`); the slab test is four-wide arithmetic; the mask and the
// keys are written with a ramp, one vector store each,
//
//     _maskN[ramp(0u, 1u, 4)] = <hit and nearer than the best>
//     _keysN[ramp(0u, 1u, 4)] = <entry distance, inf for a miss>
//
// and the sort after the loop reads them back as the vectors they are: the
// hits packed to the front, sorted by the network a switch on their count
// picks, taken out by one `permute` each, and the ones that wait written to
// the stack by one compacting store (see child-volumes-sorted.bonsai). The `&&`
// in the mask -- the slab test, and
// only where it hit, the comparison with the best -- is a merge of two
// values under a divergent branch: a `mut` the arm assigns one lane each
// and the other edge the constant, blended at the join, with the arm
// behind a uniform `any` of the mask. The children's loop itself is gone:
// it ran once, four lanes wide.
import stdlib/aabb;
import stdlib/distance;
import stdlib/intersects;
import stdlib/numerics;
import stdlib/ray;
import stdlib/triangle;

extern tris : set[Triangle];

func [[export]] trace(r : Ray) =
    argmin(|t : Triangle| distmin(r, t),
           filter(|t : Triangle| intersects(r, t), tris));

func entry(r : Ray, b : AABB) -> Float {
    interval = intersectsp_ray_aabb(r, b);
    if interval {
        extract = *interval;
        if extract.low < r.tmax && extract.high > 0.0 {
            return extract.low;
        }
    }
    return inf;
}

schedule {
    tree[[Triangle]] BVH4 =
    | Interior(children : array[BVH4, 4], lo hi : vector[vec3f, 4])
        with AABB(lo, hi) on children
    | Leaf(data : array[Triangle]) with data = data;

    tris : BVH4;

    layout tris {
        pCount : u32;
        prims : array[Triangle, pCount];
        nCount : u32;
        indirect group Nodes[nCount] row : u32 {
            children : vector[u32, 4];
            lo : vector[vec3f, 4];
            hi : vector[vec3f, 4];
        };
        group[nCount] ref : u32 {
            kind = ref & 15u;
            switch kind {
                0 => Interior from Nodes[ref >> 4];
                _ => Leaf { data = range(prims, ref >> 4, kind - 8u); };
            };
        };
    };

    // The children's loop is named by the field through the arm, and its
    // extent -- the four children -- is the gang's width.
    trace.sort(tris.Interior,
               |i : u32, r : Ray, lo : vector[vec3f, 4], hi : vector[vec3f, 4]|
               entry(r, AABB{lo[i], hi[i]}))
         .vectorize(tris.Interior.children)
         .loopify(64);
}
